"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkcybertrace_site=globalThis.webpackChunkcybertrace_site||[]).push([[130],{7735(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"welcome","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/welcome","editUrl":"https://github.com/defragedgaming/cybertrace.github.io/tree/main/blog/02/09/2026_welcome/index.md","source":"@site/blog/02/09/2026_welcome/index.md","title":"Welcome to the CyberTrace Blog","description":"What started as a personal project for my portfolio has morphed into something so much bigger: a place to learn, experiment, and understand cybersecurity through hands-on, browser-based tools and guided labs. This blog is the narrative layer that ties it all together. Here, I\'ll break down concepts, share insights from real world security work, document platform updates, and walk through the thinking that went into the tools and labs you see throughout the site.","date":"2026-02-09T14:00:12.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"cybersecurity","permalink":"/blog/tags/cybersecurity"},{"inline":true,"label":"learning","permalink":"/blog/tags/learning"},{"inline":true,"label":"updates","permalink":"/blog/tags/updates"},{"inline":true,"label":"platform","permalink":"/blog/tags/platform"}],"readingTime":3.34,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Matthew Hammel","title":"Cybersecurity Engineer & Creator of CyberTrace","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthew-hammel/","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/defragedgaming"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/defragedgaming","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthew-hammel/"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/defragedgaming.png","key":"defragedgaming"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome","title":"Welcome to the CyberTrace Blog","authors":["defragedgaming"],"tags":["cybersecurity","learning","updates","platform"]},"unlisted":false},"content":"What started as a personal project for my portfolio has morphed into something so much bigger: a place to learn, experiment, and understand cybersecurity through hands-on, browser-based tools and guided labs. This blog is the narrative layer that ties it all together. Here, I\'ll break down concepts, share insights from real world security work, document platform updates, and walk through the thinking that went into the tools and labs you see throughout the site.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether one is getting started or deep into cybersecurity, my aim is that this space should be enlightening yet easy to navigate. Cybersecurity can sometimes appear to be intimidating, but with the proper explanations and tools, it turns into something that you could also delve into confidently.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why This Blog Exists\\r\\n\\r\\nIts basis is curiosity. Every alert, every packet, every log line is full of stories. The CyberTrace blog is dedicated to helping you learn how to read them.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis blog will cover:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Explanation of security concepts with practical examples\\r\\n- Walkthroughs of laboratories and tools\\r\\n- Workflows that are actually used by SOC Analysts, Penetration Testers, and Security Engineers\\r\\n- Platform updates and announcements of new feature releases\\r\\n\\r\\n- Personal insights based on my own learning and professional experience My aspiration is to fill in this gap between theory and practice. You may not read about cybersecurity on this website; instead, you may actually learn to apply it.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## What You Can Expect\\r\\n\\r\\n### **Educational Deep Dives**\\r\\n\\r\\nSome posts will be concerned with explaining security concepts in a clear, well-structured way. Some topics covered here include:\\r\\n\\r\\n- How authentication logs can describe attacker activities\\r\\n- Why hashing algorithms matter\\r\\n- What packet headers can tell you about network activity\\r\\n\\r\\n- How defenders detect anomalies in big data These articles are designed to be comprehensible, yet also technically correct, giving you a good grounding in the subject without dumbing anything down.\\r\\n\\r\\n### **Hands-On Walkthroughs**\\r\\n\\r\\nCyberTrace is based on the principle of interactive learning. There will be many posts to guide you through:\\r\\n\\r\\n- How to use the tools available on the site\\r\\n- How to interpret the output\\r\\n\\r\\n- How these workflows map to real-world security roles If you are a learner like me, someone who likes to click, test, break, and rebuild, then these posts are right up your alley.\\r\\n\\r\\n### **Behind the Scenes**\\r\\n\\r\\nI\u2019ll also share the development perspective of CyberTrace:\\r\\n\\r\\n- How tools are designed\\r\\n- Reasons why they exist\\r\\n- What problems I\u2019m trying to solve\\r\\n\\r\\n- Lessons learned while building the platform This provides insight into the technological and artistic process used.\\r\\n\\r\\n### **Career and Skill Growth**\\r\\n\\r\\nCybersecurity is not just tools and techniques, but also a mindset. Expect posts about:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Building a strong security foundation\\r\\n- Developing analytical thinking\\r\\n- Approaching problems like a defender or attacker\\r\\n\\r\\n- Navigating the industry and learning effectively These posts are designed to help you grow not only as a practitioner but as a thinker as well.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Who This Blog Is For\\r\\n\\r\\nThis blog is intended to be read by a variety of people.\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Beginners** who need clarity and guidance\\r\\n- **Students** creating their first portfolio\\r\\n- **SOC analysts** who wish to hone their detection capabilities\\r\\n- **Penetration Testers** testing new workflows\\r\\n- **Security engineers** interested in practical tooling\\r\\n\\r\\n\u2013 **Anyone curious about how cybersecurity really works** \\r\\n    \\r\\n    If you\u2019re here to learn, you\u2019re in the right place.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## The Vision Moving Forward\\r\\n\\r\\nCybertrace is still growing, and so is this blog. Over time, you will see:\\r\\n\\r\\n- More tools\\r\\n- More labs\\r\\n- More walkthroughs\\r\\n- More real-world examples\\r\\n\\r\\nMore educational content This concept should continue to evolve, and this blog is here to track that evolution.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Final Thoughts\\r\\n\\r\\nCyber Security is an ever-evolving discipline and what defines it is that learning in the field never ends. My hope for this blog is that it might become a place where you can learn, explore, and understand the subject at your own pace. Perhaps you\'re digging through log files, playing with hashing algorithms, or learning about packet structures for the first time, and CyberTrace is here for you.\\r\\n\\r\\nThank you for being here. Let\'s create something great together."}]}}')}}]);